From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:28:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] Bind protected Fabriek bootstrap projection to server
 activation

A template can opt in to a supervisor bootstrap projection. Resume then
records a new activation on the actor, and atelet fetches a short-lived
token for it through the new WorkerService.MintSupervisorBootstrap RPC
before the workload starts. The RPC checks the actor, worker, node and
Pod identity and the template against the recorded activation. Such
templates must not capture memory, and resume refuses a memory snapshot,
so a credential read by an earlier activation never comes back.

Fork-Topic: fabriek-bootstrap
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
